## Facts to know
- Federated credentials use GitHub's immutable subject format `repo:<owner>@<id>/<repo>@<id>:…`; `setup-azure.sh` reads the repository's setting and writes the right subjects, and repairs them after a repository rename.
- The state storage account disables shared-key access; Terraform authenticates with Entra ID (`use_azuread_auth = true`, `ARM_USE_AZUREAD=true`).
- The CI/CD principal holds `Contributor` on `<% azure.resource_group %>`, `Storage Blob Data Contributor` on the state container and `AcrPush` on the registry (assigned by the foundation layer). Nothing privileged (Owner, User Access Administrator) is ever assigned by slipway.
- Check anything with: `gh secret list -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>`, `gh variable list -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>`, `gh api repos/<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>/environments/<% github.cd_environment %> --jq '.protection_rules[].type'`, `bash .slipway/setup-azure.sh` (dry run), or simply `bash <plugin>/scripts/preflight.sh`.
